  "title": "Fibonacci Number",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "contentStatus": "plus",
  "levelType": "practical",
  "statementHtml": "<p>The <strong>Fibonacci</strong> numbers, commonly denoted F(n) form a sequence, called the Fibonacci sequence, such that each number is the sum of the two preceding ones, starting from 0 and 1. That is,</p><p><br></p><ul><li>F(0) = 0, F(1) = 1</li><li>F(n) = F(n - 1) + F(n - 2), for n > 1.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Given <strong>n</strong>, calculate <strong>F(n)</strong>.</p>",
  "examples": [
    "<p><strong>Input :</strong> n = 2</p><p><strong>Output :</strong> 1</p><p><strong>Explanation :</strong> F(2) = F(1) + F(0) => 1 + 0 => 1.</p>",
    "<p><strong>Input :</strong> n = 3</p><p><strong>Output :</strong> 2</p><p><strong>Explanation :</strong> F(3) = F(2) + F(1) => 1 + 1 => 2.</p>",
    "<p><strong>Input :</strong> n = 6</p>"
  ],
  "constraintsHtml": "<ul><li>0 <= n <= 20</li></ul>",
